I ran tracert in elevated command prompt
RTT (Round Trip Time) was 60 - 250 ms for many of the hops   

I checked Control Panel/Network and Sharing Center/View your active networks/ Public network: Access type: Internet/Connections: Ethernet.
Clicked on Ethernet link  

Under General/Connection: IPv6 said Disabled.
Clicked on Properties
Selected Internet Protocol Version 4 (TCP/IPv4)
OK   

On GL-iNet Router I logged into the webpage control panel.
Selected Network on left column/IPv6
Toggled switch 'on'
Selected NAT6 from drop down menu
Selected 'automatic' for DNS acquisition method from the drop down.  

Tested result after clicking on the 'Ethernet' link
Under General/Connection: IPv6 said Disabled, again.  

I Googled and found that not all ISP allow for IPv6 for DNS
I researched for Spectrum. It was supposed to have it available if using all of their equipment, but I was using Spectrum modem with my GL-iNet BE6500 router.  

I learned online that Spectrum requires 'Native' mode instead of NAT6.
Selected 'Native'  

Tested result after clicking on the 'Ethernet' link
Under General/Connection: IPv6 it said 'Internet', meaning I had IPv6 working for Internet, now.  

Successs!
